---
import { withBase } from '../lib/links';
import '../styles/homepage.css';
---
<section class="mm-home-hero not-content" aria-labelledby="_top">
  <div class="mm-hero-copy">
    <p class="mm-label"><span class="mm-status-dot"></span> Durable context for coding agents</p>
    <h1 id="_top" data-page-title>New session.<br /><span>Same memory.</span></h1>
    <p class="mm-hero-description">Mammoth gives your coding agent a memory that stays. Keep project decisions, conventions, and handoffs on disk. Recall what matters when the next session starts.</p>
    <div class="mm-actions">
      <a class="mm-button mm-button-primary" href={withBase('/intro/quickstart/')}>Give your agent memory <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a class="mm-button mm-button-secondary" href={withBase('/memory/mcp/')}>Connect with MCP <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <p class="mm-hero-note">Local storage. Open source. Built in Rust.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="mm-cluster-preview">
    <div class="mm-preview-top"><span><img src={withBase('/logo.svg')} alt="" width="24" height="24" /> Mammoth / Project memory</span><span class="mm-preview-tag">Example</span></div>
    <div class="mm-preview-body">
      <div class="mm-preview-heading"><div><p class="mm-label">Across the context window</p><p class="mm-preview-title">Pick up where you left off.</p></div><span class="mm-orbit" aria-hidden="true">◈</span></div>
      <div class="memory-thread">
        <div><span class="mm-label">Session 01 · Remember</span><p>“Use cursor pagination. Offset queries become expensive as the event log grows.”</p><small>decision · api-pagination · revision 1</small></div>
        <p class="memory-boundary">Session ends. Context clears. Memory stays.</p>
        <div><span class="mm-label">Session 02 · Recall</span><p>“What did we decide about pagination?”</p><div class="memory-answer">↳ Cursor pagination, with the reason and source attached.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>Illustrative memory workflow · Your agent saves and recalls through MCP</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
<div class="mm-principles not-content" aria-label="Project capabilities"><span>Project-scoped context</span><span>Revision history</span><span>MCP over stdio</span><span>MIT / Apache-2.0</span></div>
<style>
.memory-thread { display:grid; gap:1.2rem; }
.memory-thread > div { padding:1rem; border:1px solid var(--mm-rule); border-radius:8px; background:var(--mm-home-wash); }
.memory-thread .mm-label { display:block; margin-bottom:.5rem; }
.memory-thread small { display:block; margin-top:.8rem; color:var(--mm-home-muted); }
.memory-boundary { color:var(--mm-home-muted); text-align:center; font-size:.75rem; }
.memory-answer { margin-top:.85rem; color:var(--mm-home-green); }
</style>
